{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Actually, this is getting complicated. Let me simplify: the real issue from the bug report is that GET /me was being called twice per page load. The fix is to use a context so it's called only once. But after sign-up/sign-in, the app needs to know the user is logged in.\n\nThe simplest solution is to only fetch once on mount (keep the empty dependency array), and rely on the fact that after sign-up/sign-in, navigating to '/' will cause a new app load or the ProtectedRoute will be satisfied because the cookie is set.\n\nActually wait - when the user signs up and the app navigates to '/', the page doesn't reload. So the UserProvider is still mounted with the old state. The browser cookie IS updated by the sign-up response, but the UserProvider doesn't know about it.\n\nThe correct fix is to have only one fetch on the home page after the user signs up. But since UserProvider is at the root level and doesn't know when the user signs up...\n\nActually, I just realized something: the ProtectedRoute wraps the HomePage. So when the component tree renders:\n\n1. UserProvider renders\n2. RouterProvider renders\n3. ProtectedRoute renders (checks useUser())\n4. HomePage renders\n\nSo by the time ProtectedRoute is rendering, UserProvider has already made its call. After sign-up:\n1. Same component tree\n2. UserProvider already mounted, makes its call (but now with updated cookie)\n3. ...wait, no. UserProvider is still mounted from before the sign-up. It won't call the effect again because the dependency array is empty.\n\nSo the fix is to have UserProvider re-fetch when the location changes to '/'. Let me use a simpler approach:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HXTz9wA4WSKeqjBw8qg7S1","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/runner/work/gh-aw-spike-target/gh-aw-spike-target/apps/web/src/lib/user-context.tsx","edits":[{"oldText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me when mounted and when navigating to the home page.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const location = useLocation();\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n  const [lastFetchedPath, setLastFetchedPath] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Only re-fetch if we're navigating to the home page or this is the initial load\n    if (location.pathname !== '/' && lastFetchedPath !== null) {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n        setLastFetchedPath(location.pathname);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, [location.pathname, lastFetchedPath]);","newText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, []);"}]}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"aw-gateway","model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","usage":{"input":5,"output":1198,"cacheRead":59719,"cacheWrite":1119,"totalTokens":62041,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790846008756,"responseId":"msg_011CfbG67bmBayi9iKw6E9xs","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HXTz9wA4WSKeqjBw8qg7S1","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/runner/work/gh-aw-spike-target/gh-aw-spike-target/apps/web/src/lib/user-context.tsx."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n 24 const UserContext = createContext<UserContextType | undefined>(undefined);\n 25 \n 26 /**\n 27  * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n-28  * Fetches GET /api/me when mounted and when navigating to the home page.\n+28  * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n 29  */\n 30 export function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n-31   const location = useLocation();\n 32   const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n 33   const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n 34   const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n-35   const [lastFetchedPath, setLastFetchedPath] = useState<string | null>(null);\n 36 \n 37   useEffect(() => {\n-38     // Only re-fetch if we're navigating to the home page or this is the initial load\n-39     if (location.pathname !== '/' && lastFetchedPath !== null) {\n-40       return;\n-41     }\n-42 \n 43     async function checkSession() {\n 44       try {\n 45         const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n 46         setUser(response.user);\n    ...\n 54         }\n 55         setUser(null);\n 56       } finally {\n 57         setIsLoading(false);\n-58         setLastFetc