{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":6,"output":1,"cacheRead":63390,"cacheWrite":586,"totalTokens":63983,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FLM2dd1FyaVzsUgHWRQ6t1","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/runner/work/gh-aw-spike-target/gh-aw-spike-target/apps/web/src/lib/user-context.tsx","edits":[{"oldText":"interface UserContextType {\n  user: User | null;\n  isLoading: boolean;\n  isSignedIn: boolean;\n}\n\nconst UserContext = createContext<UserContextType | undefined>(undefined);","newText":"interface UserContextType {\n  user: User | null;\n  isLoading: boolean;\n  isSignedIn: boolean;\n  refetch: () => Promise<void>;\n}\n\nconst UserContext = createContext<UserContextType | undefined>(undefined);"},{"oldText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <UserContext.Provider value={{ user, isLoading, isSignedIn }}>\n      {children}\n    </UserContext.Provider>\n  );\n}","newText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  const checkSession = async () => {\n    try {\n      const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n      setUser(response.user);\n      setIsSignedIn(true);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n        setIsSignedIn(false);\n      } else {\n        // For other errors, treat as signed out\n        setIsSignedIn(false);\n      }\n      setUser(null);\n    } finally {\n      setIsLoading(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    checkSession();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <UserContext.Provider value={{ user, isLoading, isSignedIn, refetch: checkSession }}>\n      {children}\n    </UserContext.Provider>\n  );\n}"}]}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me understand the e2e issue better. The tests are timing out. Let me think about what might be happening. With the changes I made, when the app first loads:\n\n1. UserProvider mounts and calls GET /me\n2. If no session, it gets 401, sets isSignedIn=false, isLoading=false\n3. ProtectedRoute checks useUser() and sees isSignedIn=false, so it redirects to /sign-in\n\nThis should work. When the user signs up:\n1. SignUpPage renders (not protected)\n2. User fills form and submits\n3. useSignUp calls POST /auth/sign-up\n4. Server returns 201 with user data and sets session cookie\n5. Component navigates to '/'\n6. ProtectedRoute renders and calls useUser()\n7. useUser() returns the context state from the initial load (before sign-up)\n8. Since that state says not signed in, it redirects to /sign-in\n\nSo the problem is exactly what I thought - the UserProvider caches the result from the first GET /me call.\n\nThe real solution is to update the UserProvider context when a user signs in or signs up. Let me create a mechanism for this. I'll add a function to UserContext that can be called to refresh the user state:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FLM2dd1FyaVzsUgHWRQ6t1","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/runner/work/gh-aw-spike-target/gh-aw-spike-target/apps/web/src/lib/user-context.tsx","edits":[{"oldText":"interface UserContextType {\n  user: User | null;\n  isLoading: boolean;\n  isSignedIn: boolean;\n}\n\nconst UserContext = createContext<UserContextType | undefined>(undefined);","newText":"interface UserContextType {\n  user: User | null;\n  isLoading: boolean;\n  isSignedIn: boolean;\n  refetch: () => Promise<void>;\n}\n\nconst UserContext = createContext<UserContextType | undefined>(undefined);"},{"oldText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <UserContext.Provider value={{ user, isLoading, isSignedIn }}>\n      {children}\n    </UserContext.Provider>\n  );\n}","newText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once per page load.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  const checkSession = async () => {\n    try {\n      const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n      setUser(response.user);\n      setIsSignedIn(true);\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n        setIsSignedIn(false);\n      } else {\n        // For other errors, treat as signed out\n        setIsSignedIn(false);\n      }\n      setUser(null);\n    } finally {\n      setIsLoading(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    checkSession();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <UserContext.Provider value={{ user, isLoading, isSignedIn, refetch: checkSession }}>\n      {children}\n    </UserContext.Provider>\n  );\n}"}]}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"aw-gateway","model":"claude-haiku-4-5-2025