 quite right. If I make the dependency array depend on location, it will re-fetch on every route change, which means it will call GET /me twice on every page load (once on mount, once when location \"changes\" after mount). Let me think about this differently.\n\nActually, the real issue is that I'm overthinking this. The problem statement says \"useMe is called twice per page load\". This was the original bug - the hook was being called twice. But the fix I made (using context) should actually fix that by only calling it once.\n\nLet me reconsider the e2e test failures. The tests are timing out waiting for elements. This suggests the page is not fully loading. Let me check if there's an actual issue with the app not starting or if it's just the tests being slow.\n\nActually, I realize the real problem: by making the dependency array `[location]`, I'm creating an infinite loop or at least a re-fetch on every navigation. Let me use a different approach - only re-fetch when navigating to a protected route like '/':"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011mN7aBe3sbrYqxMY6eB7Hc","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/runner/work/gh-aw-spike-target/gh-aw-spike-target/apps/web/src/lib/user-context.tsx","edits":[{"oldText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me once when mounted and when navigating to protected routes.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const location = useLocation();\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, [location]);","newText":"/**\n * Provides the user session to the entire app.\n * Fetches GET /api/me when mounted and when navigating to the home page.\n */\nexport function UserProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const location = useLocation();\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [isSignedIn, setIsSignedIn] = useState(false);\n  const [lastFetchedPath, setLastFetchedPath] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Only re-fetch if we're navigating to the home page or this is the initial load\n    if (location.pathname !== '/' && lastFetchedPath !== null) {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    async function checkSession() {\n      try {\n        const response = await api('/me', MeResponse);\n        setUser(response.user);\n        setIsSignedIn(true);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (error instanceof ApiClientError && error.status === 401) {\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        } else {\n          // For other errors, treat as signed out\n          setIsSignedIn(false);\n        }\n        setUser(null);\n      } finally {\n        setIsLoading(false);\n        setLastFetchedPath(location.pathname);\n      }\n    }\n\n    checkSession();\n  }, [location.pathname, lastFetchedPath]);"}]}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"aw-gateway","model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","usage":{"input":5,"output":1060,"cacheRead":58404,"cacheWrite":1315,"totalTokens":60784,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cacheWrite1h":0},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790845999724,"responseId":"msg_011CfbG5Sr7znDXc8q9xznNj","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_011mN7aBe3sbrYqxMY6eB7Hc","toolName":"edi